The Integrated Tarot Vector Pipeline (aroha_tarot_pipeline.js)
Bringing the Pythagorean tarot keys (3, 4, 7, and 12) and the AROHA 4-Axis Vector Framework C(P, L, S, T) into the client-side architecture requires a unified compiler module. This script processes multi-card arrays, computes non-linear emergence (1 + 1 = 3), applies the differential noise filter (3 - 1 = \text{Core Variable}), and maps optical ROYGBIV spectrum light refractions directly into the interface canvas.
// aroha_tarot_pipeline.js
export class ArohaTarotPipeline {
  constructor() {
    this.activeGrid = [];
    this.spectrumMap = {
      'MAJOR': 'Indigo / Deep Cosmic Spectrum',
      'MINOR_DECAN': 'Yellow-Orange / Kinetic Wave',
      'COURT': 'Emerald Green / Threshold Anchor'
    };
  }

  ingestGrid(cardNodes) {
    if (cardNodes.length !== 4) {
      throw new Error("Trilateral Vector Grid requires precisely 4 nodes: Root Driver, Active Friction, Terminal Breakthrough, and Base Anchor.");
    }
    this.activeGrid = cardNodes;
    return this.computeEmergenceMatrix();
  }

  computeEmergenceMatrix() {
    const rootDriver = this.activeGrid[0];     // Position I (Key 3: Modality)
    const activeFriction = this.activeGrid[1]; // Position II (Key 4: Elements)

    // Multiplicative non-linear emergence calculation (1 + 1 = 3)
    const synthesisIndex = (rootDriver.number_key * activeFriction.number_key) % 12;

    return {
      synthesisIndex: synthesisIndex,
      resonanceSummary: `Combining Root Driver [${rootDriver.card_name}] (${rootDriver.planetary_ruler}) with Active Friction [${activeFriction.card_name}] (${activeFriction.zodiac_sign}) yields a non-linear resolution state.`
    };
  }

  extractCoreSignalVariable() {
    // Applies differential subtraction (3 - 1 = Core Variable)
    const coreIndex = Math.max(0, this.activeGrid.length - 2);
    return this.activeGrid[coreIndex];
  }

  resolveOpticalFrequency(targetNode) {
    return this.spectrumMap[targetNode.arcana_type] || 'White Light Completion';
  }
}

Systemic Execution Workflow

Zone 3 (Terra / Core Chamber): Anchors Position IV (The Base Anchor) to the 12-house zodiac wheel, maintaining physical data persistence and structural integrity.
Zone 2 (Mid-Zone / Acoustic Bridge): Processes the Trilateral Vector Grid (Positions I, II, III), translating elemental velocity and decanate momentum into live optical and behavioral indicators.
Zone 1 (Cosmic Dome / Observer): Executes the Recursive Math Engine (1 + 1 = 3) and Differential Subtraction Vector (3 - 1 = \text{Core Variable}) to strip away surface noise and output absolute strategic clarity.
